window.docContents[68].resolve({"/Extensivity/Extensive-and-conditionally-extensive-kinds-_LPAR_Dybk___r-___13___5_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--Extensive-and-conditionally-extensive-kinds-_LPAR_Dybk___r-___13___5_RPAR_":{"contents":"\n\nA kind is extensive when, for any carving of a\nsystem into parts, the quantity of the whole equals the sum\nover the parts — the mereological structure the foundations chapter supplies.\n\nRealized as Extensive k m, a predicate over a kind k and a measurement m\n(the property value observed on each node of a Decomposition): it asserts that\nevery part is measured as a value of kind k, and that the numeral on a disjoint\nunion is the sum of the numerals on its two parts.\n\nExtensive aggregation. For an extensive kind  and a system decomposed into\nparts ,\n\nThe -quantified additivity law itself — not a single instance — is the\ndeliverable, and it is exactly what OWL2 has no vocabulary for. Builds on extensive kinds.\n\nProved in the Extensivity module by induction on the Decomposition: at a leaf\nthe law is reflexivity; at a union the single-split additive field plus the two\ninduction hypotheses give the numeral of the whole as the sum of the leaf sums.\n\nCounterexample — volume on mixing is not extensive. Volume fails the additivity\nlaw for a water/ethanol mixture: the volume of the mixture is strictly less than\nthe sum of the component volumes. Stating the negation keeps the extensive\npredicate honest. Uses extensive kinds.\n\nProved in the Extensivity module. 50 mL of water and 50 mL of ethanol measure\n96 mL when mixed; the strict inequality  is by decide, and the\nsame volMix measurement witnesses  by\nrefuting its additive field on that two-part decomposition.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Extensivity","header":"13.1. Extensive and conditionally-extensive kinds (Dybkær §13.5)","id":"/Extensivity/Extensive-and-conditionally-extensive-kinds-_LPAR_Dybk___r-___13___5_RPAR_/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--Extensive-and-conditionally-extensive-kinds-_LPAR_Dybk___r-___13___5_RPAR_"},"/Extensivity/The-interface-ledger-___-what-parts-exert-across-a-cut/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--The-interface-ledger-___-what-parts-exert-across-a-cut":{"contents":"Every measurement above reads a node of a carving. A drive torque on a hub, a contact force\nat a joint, the heat crossing a wall read no node at all: each is indexed by an ordered pair\nof parts — an interface — and a Measurement has no slot for a pair. The ledger is that slot,\nand its one law is the reason such quantities nonetheless aggregate.\n\nAn interface ledger over the parts of a carving is a pairwise\naction carrying its cancellation law as a field: the two readings of one interface sum to\nzero — for mechanical actions, Newton's third law. A pair of readings that does not cancel is\nnot two readings of one interface, so the obligation is a field for the reason a re-carving's\nwhole-preservation is.\n\nRealized as InterfaceLedger — act and antisymm — with netOn and netTotal reading\nper-part nets against a carving and mutualTotal the flow across a cut. A ledger is entered\none direction at a time: fun p q => raw p q - raw q p antisymmetrizes any raw table, and\nits law is omega. act_self is the law's own erasure clause: a carving that merges the two\nends of an interface hands both ends one name and the entry reads zero — which is why the\nrover example's two drive trains (2/2 and 3/1 hub-to-rim splits) coarsen to the same\nledger, so internal-versus-external is the carving's fact rather than the machine's —\nDybkær's observer clause (§3.3 Note 5) with a proof attached.\n\nThe exact price of additivity. For any pairwise action over a\ncarving, lawful or not, rolling up per-part nets over a union\novershoots the two halves' own rollups by precisely the two cross-flows over the cut. A\nledger that drops a reaction does not fail additivity vaguely — it fails it by this number.\nStated with no law in scope, so it is the identity a violated law is measured against.\n\nSix instances of the fold's linearity, assembled by omega. The rover example presents the\ninvoice: log the motor torques and forget the reactions, and the whole's rollup exceeds its\nhalves' by 16 — four motors' worth of uncancelled flow across the chassis–arms cut.\n\nThe rollup. Under the cancellation law the price at every cut is zero, so the sum over the\nparts of the per-part nets is the exogenous total alone. The reaction a motor induces on the\nbody is real in the per-part net — it loads a bearing — and absent from the whole; both facts\nare this theorem, read at a part and at the carving. Builds on\nthe ledger and the price identity.\n\nThe flows across any cut cancel (mutualTotal_cancel, by induction from the field), so the\ninterior of one carving cancels outright and only the exogenous column survives. In the\nrover: the chassis's net reads −16 (four motors' reactions), each hub's balances to zero, and\nthe rover's total is the ground torque alone.\n\nAdditivity, purchased. The net over a ledger satisfies the\nextensive law — but where mass's additive field is the model's free choice, this one is a\ntheorem with a hypothesis: delete the cancellation field and\nthe price identity prices exactly what remains. One predicate,\ntwo different licenses, which is the sense in which the scope of extensivity is\nkind-specific: what varies between kinds is not whether a sum appears but which law licenses\nit.\n\nBoth fields follow from the rollup: the kind is fixed by\nconstruction, and additivity collapses to the fold's union case once each rollup is its\nexogenous total. The rover example instantiates it at the torque kind, with the lawless\ncounter-witness beside it.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Extensivity","header":"13.5. The interface ledger — what parts exert across a cut","id":"/Extensivity/The-interface-ledger-___-what-parts-exert-across-a-cut/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Extensivity--The-interface-ledger-___-what-parts-exert-across-a-cut"},"/The-Interaction-Algebra-_LPAR_Flater-Appendix-C_RPAR_/The-ternary-product-of-kinds-_LPAR_Flater-App___-C_RPAR_/#interaction-algebra":{"contents":"\n\n holds when kind  times kind  yields\nkind . It is partial and curated: an application asserts the legitimate\nproducts of its kinds, each carrying the dimensional\ncoherence obligation discharged by the homomorphism theorem.\n\nRealized as the KMul field of InteractionAlgebra: a ternary relation over\ndimensioned kinds, paired in the same structure with the\nwell-formedness field kMul_coherent that requires every edge to satisfy\n. The structure cannot be formed for an\nalgebra that violates coherence.\n\n is the division dual of the kind product:  divided by  yields . Fuel-consumption \nrainfall is the classic Flater example whose careless handling yields a category\nerror rather than a number.\n\nRealized as InteractionAlgebra.KDiv, defined as the product read backwards\n(), so it inherits the same\npartiality and coherence side-condition.\n\nMultiplication and division are inverse on kinds. A product and its quotient\nhold together — the round-trip is an equivalence:\n\nTogether with dimensional coherence this is the\ncalculus that OWL2 cannot host: an algebraic law with arithmetic side-conditions,\nproved rather than consistency-checked. Builds on the kind product and the kind quotient.\n\nImmediate from defining KDiv as the converse of KMul: the biconditional is\nIff.rfl. The round-trip is the symmetry of that definition.\n\nWorked instance. Torque times plane angle is energy, and energy is not torque,\neven though . Formally\n holds while\n — the small example that shows the algebra\ncarrying information dimension alone discards. Uses the kind product.\n\nProved in the Interaction module. torque, angle (dimension one), and\nenergy are declared as dimensioned kinds, with torque and energy both given\ndimension force · length; the product edge torque_angle_energy is asserted in\nthe worked siMech algebra and its coherence checked by the Dimension-group\ncomputation, while energy.kind ≠ torque.kind is by decide.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009The Interaction Algebra (Flater Appendix C)","header":"11.1. The ternary product of kinds (Flater App. C)","id":"/The-Interaction-Algebra-_LPAR_Flater-Appendix-C_RPAR_/The-ternary-product-of-kinds-_LPAR_Flater-App___-C_RPAR_/#interaction-algebra"}});